+Minecraft 26.2 / mapped 1.21.11 input hook verification
+
+Primary mapped API references checked 2026-08-01:
+- net.minecraft.client.player.KeyboardInput extends ClientInput and overrides public void tick().
+- ClientInput exposes public Input keyPresses and protected Vec2 moveVector.
+- net.minecraft.world.entity.player.Input is a seven-boolean record:
+  forward, backward, left, right, jump, shift, sprint.
+- Vec2 movement convention is x = left impulse, y = forward impulse.
+
+Implementation boundary:
+- Inject into KeyboardInput#tick() at RETURN.
+- Preserve jump, shift, and sprint from the freshly sampled Input record.
+- Replace only movement booleans and moveVector while MovementOverrideState is active.
+- Do not construct movement packets; LocalPlayer consumes the adjusted vanilla ClientInput.
+
+References:
+https://mappings.dev/1.21.11/net/minecraft/client/player/KeyboardInput.html
+https://mappings.dev/1.21.11/net/minecraft/client/player/ClientInput.html
+https://mappings.dev/1.21.11/net/minecraft/world/entity/player/Input.html
+
+Local targeted verification:
+- Compiled the real movement-frame classes, ClientInput accessor, and KeyboardInput mixin
+  against minimal stubs matching the mapped 26.2 field/method signatures.
+- Result: Java compilation passed on 2026-08-01.
+- Full Fabric remap/runtime validation remains required in Java 25 CI.
